<title>CHINA: China soy imports up in January-October.</title>
<headline>China soy imports up in January-October.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's imports of soybeans, soymeal and soybean oil all rose in the first 10 months compared with the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Following are details of imports as well as exports with all figures in tonnes -</p>
<p>IMPORTS</p>
<p>		    OCT	  JAN-OCT	 COMPARED WITH</p>
<p>						     JAN-OCT 1995</p>
<p> Soybeans    38,967.9     689,158.9    +    363 percent</p>
<p> Soymeal    328,479.1   1,255,405.0    + 12,019 percent</p>
<p> Soybean oil 79,014.1   1,052,620.7    + 5 percent</p>
<p>EXPORTS</p>
<p>		    OCT	  JAN-OCT	 COMPARED WITH</p>
<p>						     JAN-OCT 1995</p>
<p> Soybeans    2,254.7     149,797.0	  - 50.2 percent</p>
<p> Soymeal     1,774.6	65,554.2	  - 92.4 percent</p>
<p> Soybean oil   243.7	 3,277.6	  - 42.3 percent</p>
</text>
